    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Direct overhead Sun rays hit the Tropic of Cancer during Summer Solstice (June 21) and Tropic of Capricorn during Winter Solstice (December 22).",
        "Equal day and night duration occurs globally during Vernal Equinox (March 21) and Autumnal Equinox (September 23).",
        "Perihelion occurs around January 3 when Earth is closest to the Sun, while Aphelion occurs around July 4 when Earth is farthest."
